href: https://xwiki.ewi.tudelft.nl/xwiki/rest/wikis/sce2026group04/spaces/tmp%3A%20Pitch/spaces/1%20Foundation/spaces/a2%20Stakeholders/spaces/a2.1%20Mindful%20Walk/pages/WebHome
title: a2.1 Mindful Walk
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Seven stakeholders. Three talk on the walk: the resident (ST-01), a fellow resident (ST-02), a relative on the phone (ST-03). Two support it: the care worker, who answers alerts and painful questions (ST-04), and the activity coordinator, who keeps pairs, settings and the relationship map (ST-05). Two set limits: medical and therapy staff (ST-06) and management (ST-07). Shared: the resident's well-being and trust. Divided on: freedom against safety, and how much the System may know and pass on.

= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-01
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-05.
|Type|Direct - walks, talks, consents, sets own preferences
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - company, a chat
* HV-02 Dignity (high) - slips not remarked on; never walked like a pet
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - the truth, from someone trusted
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - own reasons, own settings, own consent
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - own conversations and secrets
* HV-07 Identity (high) - own past, own words
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - fresh air, calm
* HV-04 Safety (medium) - no falls, no getting lost
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Walks with ST-02, or talks with ST-03 on the phone. Helped by ST-04. Agrees settings with ST-05. Walking assessed by ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-01 to SA-04; asks-in → SA-05; holds → HV-01 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-03; elaborated-as → HP-01, HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Fellow resident [ST-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-02
|Name|Fellow resident (walking partner)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-02, SA-04.
|Type|Direct - walks and talks with ST-01; often has dementia too
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - a mate to talk to
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - free to decline or end a walk
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - own secrets stay with own System
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - own walk, own health
* HV-02 Dignity (medium) - a partner, not a minder
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Matched with ST-01 by ST-05; both consent. Own relatives, own care plan, own copy of the System.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-02, SA-04; holds → HV-01 to HV-03, HV-05, HV-06; appears-in → PS-01; elaborated-as → HP-01, HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Relative [ST-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-03
|Name|Relative
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-03 to SA-05.
|Type|Direct on calls - talks, receives hints. Indirect - tells the life story; agrees settings and answers.
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - contact between visits
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - no lies told to their relative
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - their relative calm after a call
* HV-07 Identity (high) - their relative stays the person they knew
* HV-03 Privacy (low) - may want to know more than the resident would share
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Calls ST-01. Gives life story and sensitive topics to ST-05. Agrees with ST-04 who answers what. May consent on ST-01's behalf.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-03; supports → SA-04, SA-05; holds → HV-03, HV-05 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-02, PS-03; elaborated-as → HP-03 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Care worker [ST-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-04
|Name|Care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-05.
|Type|Direct - starts walks, answers alerts; trusted person for named sensitive topics
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - every resident back, unharmed
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - one agreed answer from all staff
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - residents out, and calm
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - for residents; no surveillance of own work
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Trusted person for named topics of named residents. Keeps the relationship map current with ST-05. Follows ST-06 on walking and medical news.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-05; supports → SA-01 to SA-04; holds → HV-03 to HV-05, HV-08; appears-in → PS-01, PS-03; elaborated-as → HP-04 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Activity coordinator [ST-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-05
|Name|Activity coordinator
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-02, SA-05.
|Type|Direct - keeps profiles, pairs, per-person settings and the relationship map
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - pairs that work
* HV-07 Identity (high) - profiles that fit the person
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - map and profiles in their care
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium) - settings agreed with the resident
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Writes profiles with ST-01 and ST-03. Pairs ST-01 and ST-02. Reviews the map with ST-04 after each event. Employed by ST-07.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-02, SA-05; holds → HV-01, HV-03, HV-06, HV-07.

= Stakeholder - Medical and therapy staff [ST-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-06
|Name|Medical and therapy staff: physician, nurse, physiotherapist, psychologist
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-05.
|Type|Indirect - assess fall risk and walking alone; set walk length; tell medical news
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - fall risk
* HV-05 Well-being (high)
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - a diagnosis is told by them
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - medical confidentiality
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Assess ST-01 and ST-02. Advise ST-04 and ST-05. Trusted person for medical topics.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01, SA-05; holds → HV-03 to HV-05, HV-08.

= Stakeholder - Care home management [ST-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-07
|Name|Care home management
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01.
|Type|Indirect - data controller; exits; local network; decides on adoption
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - liable for falls and exits
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - GDPR, health data
* HV-05 Well-being (medium) - quality of care
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-04 and ST-05. Responsible for the garden, the exits and the local server.

== Graph edges ==

governs → SA-01 (exits), System data (local only); holds → HV-03 to HV-05.
